=== A. The Fibonacci-anyon braid IS a complex Fibonacci recurrence ===
 normalised braid b=cB obeys b^2 = a b + 1 : True   with a = (-0-1.175571j)  a^2 = phi-3: True
 Millington's Q=[[1,1],[1,0]] obeys Q^2 = 1*Q + 1 (a=1). det Q = -1 ; det b = (-1+0j)
 complex Fibonacci f_n: Cassini f(n-1)f(n+1)-f(n)^2 = (-1)^n for n=1..24: True
 |f_n| for n=0..10: [0.     1.     1.1756 0.382  0.7265 1.2361 0.7265 0.382  1.1756 1.
 0.    ]  (bounded/periodic: elliptic, vs Q hyperbolic)
 mirror hand uses R*: a* = (-0+1.175571j)  -> f_n -> conj(f_n), Cassini sign unchanged

=== golden chain, L=10, Hilbert dim 123 (Lucas number L_10 = 123) ===
 P_i projectors: True  braids unitary: True  Yang-Baxter B_i B_i+1 B_i = B_i+1 B_i B_i+1: True
 chiral term C is Hermitian and purely imaginary (odd under i->-i): True True  |C|= 14.872

